{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "008R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y$", "MATH_0005": "$Y$", "MATH_0006": "\\begin{eqnarray*}\nf_* : \\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_X) &\n\\longrightarrow &\n\\textit{Mod}(f_*\\mathcal{O}_X) \\\\\nf^{-1} : \\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_Y) &\n\\longrightarrow &\n\\textit{Mod}(f^{-1}\\mathcal{O}_Y)\n\\end{eqnarray*}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fee0895d61ee4757e1a2109d9a38d1111c52fc6a3ba5426a5fec936666fd85fd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8c7441244a9dc537bc68d9e201f266181e182b2cafb288304918f1df373a9582", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a continuous map.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a sheaf of rings on <MATH_0003> and\nlet <MATH_0004> be a sheaf of rings on <MATH_0005>.\nSo now we have defined functors\n<MATH_0006>\nThese satisfy some compatibilities as follows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b5c1db4953b4676efa26abb8aa8dc81bb438ac157bbd9620fa561e1d6cf8a112", "unit_id": "tag:008R:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "008R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$f^{-1}\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\Mor_{\\textit{Mod}(f^{-1}\\mathcal{O})}(f^{-1}\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F})\n=\n\\Mor_{\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O})}(\\mathcal{G}, f_*\\mathcal{F}).\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{O} \\to f_*f^{-1}\\mathcal{O}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-pullback-module}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-pushforward-module}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-adjoint-push-pull-modules}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:56d8f365ae3b800475dd9edcaaa47836fe360d5634494aca78841d969b9a05fa", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7ab17fcd1d1c09af5c595ce463a061d677a45ffd43bf113bfc687cec48d2914b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a continuous map of topological spaces.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a sheaf of rings on <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a sheaf of <MATH_0005>-modules.\nLet <MATH_0006> be a sheaf of <MATH_0007>-modules.\nThen\n<MATH_0008>\nHere we use\nLemmas <REF_0001>\nand <REF_0002>, and we think of\n<MATH_0009> as an <MATH_0010>-module by restriction via\n<MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9c5b0835fd037da1cb3c12ee6dfae5ccc52e0873cc2d7a380a3eba7c68141e24", "unit_id": "tag:008Y:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "008R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "\\begin{eqnarray*}\n\\Mor_{\\textit{Mod}(f^{-1}\\mathcal{O})}(f^{-1}\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F})\n& = &\n\\Mor_{\\textit{Mod}(f_p\\mathcal{O})}(f_p\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F}) \\\\\n& = &\n\\Mor_{\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O})}(\\mathcal{G}, f_*\\mathcal{F}).\n\\end{eqnarray*}", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-adjoint-push-pull-presheaves-modules}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-sheafification-presheaf-modules}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9215db3548f1b3f4fc1777550611337311f8f94ae601cdde1600887acf9263de", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2c79c12f87421d31880c6d9e73cd1da611d24af7aa5cde4f0e090c8113c9235c", "source_text": "Argue by the equalities\n<MATH_0001>\nwhere the second is\nLemmas <REF_0001>\nand the first is by Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e6eca1d934c29e8089b9d1f5c8f433c2cd23689054c976ce8587f31a7490248a", "unit_id": "tag:008Y:proof"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "008R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0007": "$f_*\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\Mor_{\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O})}(\n\\mathcal{O} \\otimes_{f^{-1}f_*\\mathcal{O}} f^{-1}\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F})\n=\n\\Mor_{\\textit{Mod}(f_*\\mathcal{O})}(\\mathcal{G}, f_*\\mathcal{F}).\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$f^{-1}f_*\\mathcal{O} \\to \\mathcal{O}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-pullback-module}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-pushforward-module}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-adjoint-pull-push-modules}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8a7148f9a0d52cd383792c3fd1d89836290237473673886aa31ffdc5e32a6df3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2866eca5ff3ae48f2cc91d94e60b482011224ffae7e2a73a84b06b33778011c7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a continuous map of topological spaces.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a sheaf of rings on <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a sheaf of <MATH_0005>-modules.\nLet <MATH_0006> be a sheaf of <MATH_0007>-modules.\nThen\n<MATH_0008>\nHere we use\nLemmas <REF_0001>\nand <REF_0002>, and we use\nthe canonical map <MATH_0009>\nin the definition of the tensor product.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:eba347bef70a0129a6c993b5b1de6b26aa474f378180a0e6bdf089b2a4822eb9", "unit_id": "tag:008Z:statement"}
